{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "framework": "playwright",
  "testId": "testim-migrated/tests/webstore/plp/verify-facets-and-their-filters.spec.ts > PLP - Verify Facets and Their Filters > verify facets and their filters on Plumbing category",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Guest opens the Plumbing PLP, checks the Spout Type, Material Type and ToeStyle facet headings, expands them and checks facet values and product counts, filters by Spout Type = Mid Arc (3 of 3 results) and checks the three products' names, SKUs and retail prices, clears the filters, checks the first product and the Material Type values/counts, then applies ToeStyle = Carbonmax. Read-only.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the webstore as a guest and open Plumbing via Departments (gotoCategory('linkPlumbing')).",
      "Check facet headings SpoutType, PlumbingPartsMaterial and ToeStyle; expand the three facets.",
      "Check SpoutType values Mid Arc / Low Arc and their counts.",
      "Click Mid Arc; check 'Showing 3' and 'of 3 Results'.",
      "Check name, SKU and retail price of products 176, 177 and 178 and that product 176's details are visible.",
      "Clear all facets; check the first product name and the Material Type heading.",
      "Re-expand Material Type; check values PVC, Cast Iron, Nickel and their counts.",
      "Expand ToeStyle and click Carbonmax; check the results bar is visible."
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "category",
      "product",
      "product_attributes",
      "store"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [],
    "assertions": [
      "Facet headings show their labels (Spout Type, Material Type, ToeStyle).",
      "Facet values show their labels and product counts (Mid Arc 3, Low Arc 1, PVC 9, Cast Iron 4, Nickel 1).",
      "Filtering by Mid Arc shows 'Showing 3 ... of 3 Results' and the three matching products with name, SKU and retail price.",
      "After Clear All the first listed product is the recorded one and the result count is no longer 'of 3'."
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Title 'verify facets and their filters on Plumbing category' and the ten step labels match the flow; guest storageState; no linked AIO cases.",
      "All JSON data comes through loadData(FacetsDataSchema, rawData, ...) (spec line 39). toeCarbonmax/toeCarbonmaxCount are in the schema but not in the scan (unused by the spec); Carbonmax is a literal at line 196 that the scanner did not list.",
      "Profile (atstage 2026-11-01): Z-1235102 FOUND active SimpleProduct (MountainPlumbing), inventory 4842, storefrontProductIndex 0; z-1235803 and z-1235804 FOUND active SimpleProducts, inventory 5000, storefront index 1; productName FOUND as z-1234595 (MountainPlumbing). tda rows: Faucets (ZnodeCategoryId 85, parent 83) holds products 175-183, which include 176-178.",
      "Store MaxwellsHardware: the store every migrated webstore spec runs on; not named in the scan.",
      "CATEGORY_WITH_PRODUCTS (pending) now covers the Plumbing PLP the test opens from Departments: need category {store, topLevel true, minProducts 4}; the link id linkPlumbing (config) is built from category.name.",
      "CATEGORY_FACET_VALUES (pending) now covers the facets: need facets {store, categoryId @category.categoryId, attributeCodes SpoutType,PlumbingPartsMaterial,ToeStyle (the attribute codes the test reads, in order), minValuesPerAttribute 2, minProductsForValue 3, maxProductsForValue 3 (the test checks exactly three filtered products)}. Values are ordered by product count, highest first. Facet headings -> facet1Label..facet3Label; Mid Arc 3 / Low Arc 1 -> facet1Value1Label/Count, facet1Value2Label/Count; PVC 9, Cast Iron 4, Nickel 1 -> facet2Value1..3Label/Count; the three filtered products (first value of the first facet) -> filteredProduct1..3Name / Sku / RetailPrice (prices shown as currency), ordered by product id.",
      "Gap (params): minValuesPerAttribute is one minimum for all three attributes, but the test reads 2 SpoutType values, 3 Material Type values and 1 ToeStyle value (Carbonmax, line 196, not scanned; facet3Value1Label / facet3Value1Code). With 2, the third Material Type value (Nickel, facet2Value3*) is not guaranteed and ToeStyle must have 2 values although the test reads one; a per-attribute minimum needs a key change (human decides).",
      "Built by the spec from outputs, roles unchanged: 'Showing 3' and 'of 3 Results' (expected-output) from facets.filteredCount; the facet value test ids MidArc/midArc, LowArc/lowArc, PVC/pvc, CastIron/castIron, Nickel/nickel (config) from facet<N>Value<M>Code (assumes the value code is the test id; reviewer to confirm); the product test ids hdgProductName176.. / spnProductSkuValue176.. / spnRetailPrice176.. / divProductDetails176 (config) from filteredProduct1..3ProductId. The facet heading codes SpoutType, PlumbingPartsMaterial, ToeStyle are the attributeCodes param (config).",
      "Not covered: the first product after Clear All (productName, 'Mountain Plumbing 4 Inch Round ...') stays expected-output: the default sort comes from the search index, so no key can produce it (CATEGORY_LISTING_SORT_ANCHORS gives only the Name sorts).",
      "Data in code: product ids 176/177/178 in test ids (hdgProductName176, spnProductSkuValue176, spnRetailPrice176, divProductDetails176, ...), the category link linkPlumbing and the 'Showing 3' / 'of 3 Results' literals.",
      "migrate: loadData is used, but the asserted counts and prices depend on the data (swap rule 3) and product ids and facet codes are in the spec code (swap rule 4).",
      "2026-11-02: minValuesPerAttribute 2 -> 1 (user decision): one value applies to all three attributes and ToeStyle has a single value in Plumbing, so with 2 no category qualified; the test's reads of a 2nd/3rd value of an attribute are no longer guaranteed by the key."
    ],
    "confidence": "low",
    "needsReview": true
  },
  "requires": [
    {
      "key": "CATEGORY_WITH_PRODUCTS",
      "alias": "category",
      "params": {
        "store": "MaxwellsHardware",
        "minProducts": 4,
        "topLevel": true
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "CATEGORY_FACET_VALUES",
